## 🧪 SERIALIZER VALIDATION ENTERPRISE ARCHITECTURE

### 🎯 JAVA-STYLE VALIDATION PATTERN

**PRINCIPLE**: Treat Django serializers like Java RequestEntity validation layer

#### 🏗️ LAYERED VALIDATION ARCHITECTURE:

```python
# ✅ CORRECT: Enterprise Validation Layering

# LAYER 1: SERIALIZER (Input Validation Only)
class EpisodeCreateSerializer(serializers.Serializer):
    """
    Handles basic input validation - equivalent to Java @Valid annotations
    """
    title = serializers.CharField(max_length=200)
    duration = serializers.IntegerField(min_value=1)

    def validate(self, data):
        # ONLY basic field validation - no model calls
        if not data.get('title', '').strip():
            raise serializers.ValidationError("Title cannot be empty")
        return data

# LAYER 2: SERIALIZER-SERVICE (Model-Based Validation)
class EpisodeSerializerService:
    """
    MANDATORY: Serializers MUST use SerializerService for all model operations
    Handles model-dependent validation logic for serializers
    """

    def __init__(self, episode_service: EpisodeServiceInterface):
        self._episode_service = episode_service

    def validate_episode_business_rules(self, data: dict) -> ValidationResult:
        # ALL model operations go through service layer - NO direct model access
        if self._episode_service.episode_exists_by_title(data['title']):
            return ValidationResult(False, ["Episode title already exists"])

        # Cross-entity validation through service
        if not self._episode_service.category_exists(data['category_id']):
            return ValidationResult(False, ["Invalid category"])

        return ValidationResult(True, [])

# LAYER 3: SERVICE (Business Logic)
class EpisodeService(EpisodeServiceInterface):
    """
    ONLY layer that can access models directly
    Handles complex business logic and orchestration
    """

    def __init__(self, episode_repository: EpisodeRepositoryInterface):
        self._episode_repository = episode_repository

    def create_episode(self, validated_data: dict) -> Episode:
        # Business logic implementation - direct model access allowed ONLY here
        return self._episode_repository.create(validated_data)

    def episode_exists_by_title(self, title: str) -> bool:
        """Service method for other layers to check episode existence"""
        return self._episode_repository.exists_by_title(title)

    def category_exists(self, category_id: int) -> bool:
        """Service method for other layers to check category existence"""
        return self._episode_repository.category_exists(category_id)
```

